# One repository, two operating systems. Git for Windows defaults to
# core.autocrlf=true, which would rewrite every line on checkout and hand the
# Linux side a diff of the entire tree on the way back. Normalise to LF in the
# repository and check out LF everywhere; Python, Qt and MSVC all read it fine.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Shell scripts must keep LF or bash refuses them outright.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Windows-native scripts are the one exception.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf

# Never touch binaries (the prebuilt demo programs included).
*.exe binary
*.dll binary
*.so binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.ico binary
demo_module/Linux/x11-native/x11-native binary
